  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts`. It typechecks, but I could not run it or `vite build` here, so I haven't seen a rendered frame.\n\n- **Island:** the terrain is generated from code as separate triangles with face normals, so it renders flat-shaded. Triangles are coloured by height (sand, grass, dry grass, rock). About 24 trees (a trunk plus two cones) and 11 faceted rocks sit on it, and a fixed seed makes the layout the same on every load.\n- **Water:** a custom shader material with vertex waves and flat-shaded facets. The colour follows the sky and shifts from shallow to deep. It has a sun or moon glint and animated foam along the shore, and it fades into the sky colour at a distance. The foam and shallow tint come from the island's height baked into the water mesh. A `waveClock` uniform animates it every frame.\n- **Day/night:** a full cycle takes 20 seconds, and it starts at 9:00. `?hour=14` in the URL freezes the clock. Each frame it moves the Preetham sky sun (with stars) and the sun and moon lights. It changes sun colour and intensity, and the hemisphere fill light's colour and intensity (its ground colour stays fixed). Sunrise and sunset are warmer. The moon and the fill light keep the scene lit at night.\n- **Camera:** it orbits the island slowly at about 17 m up and 37 m out, one lap per 80 seconds. The orbit uses `app.camera?.setPose`, which I haven't seen run. If `app.camera` is undefined at runtime, the camera stays at its starting position, which still frames the island.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after the second frame callback. A fallback sets it after `app.ready()` and two animation frames.\n\n",
